{"timestamp": "2026-11-18T01:55:53.906359-05:00", "id": "56b351cf5e5042858151f515c743dc0a", "skill": "ui-ux-review", "label": "UI/UX review", "provider": "opencode", "model": "opencode-go/hy4-flash-free", "effort": "default", "status": "running", "started": "2026-11-18 01:55:53", "command": "/Users/roosevelt/.opencode/bin/opencode run --standalone -m opencode-go/hy4-flash-free 'Apply the ui-ux-pro-max skill to this task:\nReview the dashboard-app Run tab (templates/pages/run.html, static/app.js and static/style.css). Read the skill'\"'\"'s applicable reference files. Report at most five concrete findings with file:line citations; do not edit any file.\n\nResolve the skill'\"'\"'s relative reference and script paths against /Volumes/SANDISK USB/work/Cloudtransition/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max.\n\nSkill instructions (/Volumes/SANDISK USB/work/Cloudtransition/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md):\n---\nname: ui-ux-pro-max\ndescription: \"UI/UX design intelligence. 50 styles, 21 palettes, 50 font pairings, 20 charts, 9 stacks (React, Next.js, Vue, Svelte, SwiftUI, React Native, Flutter, Tailwind, shadcn/ui). Actions: plan, build, create, design, implement, review, fix, improve, optimize, enhance, refactor, check UI/UX code. Projects: website, landing page, dashboard, admin panel, e-commerce, SaaS, portfolio, blog, mobile app, .html, .tsx, .vue, .svelte. Elements: button, modal, navbar, sidebar, card, table, form, chart. Styles: glassmorphism, claymorphism, minimalism, brutalism, neumorphism, bento grid, dark mode, responsive, skeuomorphism, flat design. Topics: color palette, accessibility, animation, layout, typography, font pairing, spacing, hover, shadow, gradient. Integrations: shadcn/ui MCP for component search and examples.\"\n---\n\n# UI/UX Pro Max - Design Intelligence\n\nComprehensive design guide for web and mobile applications. Contains 50+ styles, 97 color palettes, 57 font pairings, 99 UX guidelines, and 25 chart types across 9 technology stacks. Searchable database with priority-based recommendations.\n\n## When to Apply\n\nReference these guidelines when:\n- Designing new UI components or pages\n- Choosing color palettes and typography\n- Reviewing code for UX issues\n- Building landing pages or dashboards\n- Implementing accessibility requirements\n\n## How to Use\n\nSearch specific domains using the CLI tool below.\n\n## Routing\n\n| Task / job | Read |\n| --- | --- |\n| Which rule categories apply, and their priority quick reference | `rules-by-priority.md` |\n| Python is missing or must be installed | `setup-python-prerequisites.md` |\n| Run a UI/UX request: analyze, generate design system, supplement searches, stack guidelines | `design-workflow.md` |\n| Persist the design system (MASTER.md + page overrides) | `persist-design-system.md` |\n| Look up search domains, stacks, output formats, search tips | `search-reference.md` |\n| See a worked end-to-end example | `example-workflow.md` |\n| Fix commonly overlooked unprofessional UI (icons, hover, contrast, spacing) | `common-rules-professional-ui.md` |\n| Verify UI code before delivery | `pre-delivery-checklist.md` |\n\nRead only the file that matches the current task; do not load every file.\n'", "output": null, "duration": null, "preview": null}
